From a1c6afd3a9fde3861e71e79d3e674bee7cc3476c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:13:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hardening-2): kill ACAO wildcard, decouple readiness
 gate, harden CI, validate env

Production probe after the P0 deploy surfaced three defects:

1. ACAO:* on document responses. The app never sets this header, so the
   wildcard originates upstream (Vercel project config or a DNS-layer proxy).
   vercel.json/next.config now set Access-Control-Allow-Origin explicitly to
   the canonical origin, which replaces any same-named header at the edge.
   verify.sh additionally prints the attribution probe when it sees a wildcard.
   Also adds Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin and X-DNS-Prefetch-Control.

2. verify.sh gated the readiness section on $fail -eq 0, so a header
   regression silently hid the legal-compliance and commerce checks. The two
   axes are now independent: contract failures no longer suppress readiness.
   Readiness gains an anti-lying invariant (no card/SEPA/wallet chips without
   a real checkout) and a Cal.com booking assertion.

3. CI/quality failed on PR #2. The workflow's inline curl assertions
   duplicated verify.sh and depended on wait-on plus CHROMEWEBDRIVER probing.
   CI now runs 'npm run verify' - one acceptance contract, identical locally,
   in CI and against production - with a dependency-free readiness poll and a
   guaranteed server teardown. Adds concurrency cancellation.

Also: scripts/env-push.sh validates and pushes production env vars
non-interactively. 'vercel env add' accepts an empty value and reports
success, which is how all seven production vars were stored empty; this
script refuses empty values and malformed Stripe/Cal/Resend/email formats.
Adds sharp for real AVIF/WebP encoding under next start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019GWsiUVmM3mLw1X2wD6eJi
